# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the concurrency suite.
#
# crossbeam-epoch's epoch-advance (Global::try_advance) synchronizes via an
# asymmetric membarrier fence that ThreadSanitizer does not model as a
# happens-before edge. Under -Zbuild-std (crossbeam fully instrumented) this
# yields false-positive data-race reports on crossbeam's OWN garbage-collection
# reclamation: the deferred free of an internal Local handle or SealedBag queue
# node racing a concurrent Global::collect/try_advance read. Every flagged
# address belongs to crossbeam's GC structures, never to polyplug memory, so
# polyplug's epoch-protected read path is unaffected. Matches crossbeam's own
# upstream ci/tsan suppression.
race:crossbeam_epoch
